WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.680
ALICIA WILLIAMS: Today,
we're talking about I/O,

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.760
returning to the office with
Chrome, and a few AI updates.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.580
I'm Alicia, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.450
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.910
We've all been working
from home for a while now.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.560
And as we get back
to the office,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.860
Chrome OS will help us make
that a seamless transition.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.710
At Google, we'll be moving
to a hybrid workweek

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.930
where most Googlers spend
approximately three days

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.260
in the office and two days
wherever they work best.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.440
It's no surprise that as the
modern secure cloud-first

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.890
platform, Chrome OS is playing
a key role in our transition

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.630
to a hybrid work model.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.630
Because Chrome OS devices
can easily be shared,

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:46.310
more flexible working models
and spaces are now possible.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.110
We're excited to
announce that we've

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.780
made contacts in
our AI even stronger

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.710
with Agent Assist for chat,
now in public preview.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.930
Agent Assist provides
your human agents

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.330
with continuous support
during their calls,

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:02.810
and now chats, by identifying
the customer's intent

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.300
and providing them with
real time recommendations,

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.630
such as articles and
FAQs, as well as responses

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.210
to customer messages to
more effectively resolve

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.060
the conversation.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.940
PyTorch is an open source
machine learning and deep

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.880
learning library
predominantly used in research

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.280
and has gained tremendous
traction in the industry

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.340
as well due to its ease
of use and deployment.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.800
Google Cloud AI platform
is a fully managed

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.350
end-to-end platform for data
science and machine learning

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.760
on Google Cloud.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.210
In this new series of blog
posts, PyTorch on Google Cloud,

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:38.240
we aim to share how to
build, train, and deploy

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.030
PyTorch models at
scale and how to create

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:44.990
reproducible machine learning
pipelines on Google Cloud.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:46.550
I/O was last week.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.110
And if you missed
the virtual event,

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.970
be sure to check out
the technical talks

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:53.660
on your favorite
product YouTube pages.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.760
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.320
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.630
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.620
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.210
We'll see you in the cloud.

